      "text": [
        " رِوَايَةِ مُعَاوِيَةَ بْنِ عَمَّارٍ عَنْهُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ قَالَ : «اَلْكَسِيرُ يُحْمَلُ فَيَرْمِي اَلْجِمَارَ وَ اَلْمَبْطُونُ يُرْمَى عَنْهُ وَ يُصَلَّى عَنْهُ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2822 - In a narration by Muawiyah ibn Ammar from Imam Abu Abdullah (as):\n\"The injured person (who cannot walk) should be carried to throw the pebbles at the Jamara, while for the person afflicted with severe illness (such as diarrhea), the stoning can be done on their behalf, and prayers can also be performed on their behalf.\""
        ]
      }
    },
